        "original_id": "8d43f7f7-cff4-5a23-a596-c234875dfac7",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Alvin Lee, Chad Gray\n- Bands: Ten Years After, Hellyeah, Mudvayne, Nonpoint\n- Products: Nineteen Ninety-Four, I Hear You Rockin', Miracle\n\nFacts:\n- Alvin Lee, born Graham Anthony Barnes on 19 December 1944 and died on 6 March 2013, was an English singer and guitarist.\n- Alvin Lee was best known as the lead vocalist and lead guitarist of the blues rock band Ten Years After.\n- Chad Gray was born on October 16, 1971.\n- Chad Gray was the lead vocalist for the American heavy metal band Mudvayne and later became the lead vocalist for the groove metal supergroup Hellyeah.\n- Nineteen Ninety-Four is a 1994 album by Alvin Lee.\n- Nineteen Ninety-Four was released in the United States as I Hear You Rockin'.\n- The song Miracle by Nonpoint features Chad Gray contributing vocals during the chorus, and the appearance identifies him with Mudvayne fame.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "c6261c25-4b2d-57a8-95ac-17ce2f66571d",
        "text": "Page: Alvin Lee. Sentence: Alvin Lee (born Graham Anthony Barnes; 19 December 1944 – 6 March 2013) was an English singer and guitarist, best known as the lead vocalist and lead guitarist of the blues rock band Ten Years After.\nPage: Chad Gray. Sentence: Chad Gray (born October 16, 1971), is the lead vocalist for the groove metal supergroup Hellyeah and former lead vocalist for American heavy metal band Mudvayne.\nPage: Nineteen Ninety-Four (album). Sentence: Nineteen Ninety-Four (Viceroy VIC 8012-2, Reissue: Repertoire REP5191) is a 1994 album by Alvin Lee released in the United States as I Hear You Rockin'\nPage: Miracle (Nonpoint song). Sentence: It features Chad Gray of Mudvayne fame contributing vocals during the song's chorus.",
